!!!OTL: Les deux noyés de Tignish
!!!SNG: Léo J. Gallant
!!!COM: Madame Pierre Poirier (Isabelle Gaudet)
!!!AGN: Complainte
!!!ARE: Tignish, Prince Edward Island, Canada
!!!YER: 1973
!!!SRC: Georges Arsenault, Complaintes acadiennes de l'Île-du-Prince-Édouard (Montréal: Leméac, 1980), p. 225; Coll. Georges Arsenault, enreg. 451.
!!!ONB: Georges Arsenault collected this song from Léo J. Gallant in June 1973. Gallant was born in Tignish and later lived in Arichat, Nova Scotia. He learned the song from Isabelle Gaudet, who is credited with writing it. The song tells the story of a drowning tragedy and uses the tune of "Noces - Adieu de la mariée".
